BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[Geophysics Department] Geophysics PhD Defense\, Becca Prentice: "
 Utilizing Transient Electromagnetic Method to Locate Pathways for River-So
 urced Recharge in the San Joaquin Valley"
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261106T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261106T140000
DTSTAMP:20261106T195215Z
UID:stanford_campus-localist-54408464681298-54408473948828@local-events
DESCRIPTION:The importance of water is becoming increasingly apparent acro
 ss the globe. As more regions experience swings in climate\, from extreme 
 dry periods to extreme wet periods\, there is growing recognition of the i
 mportance of storing excess water during wet periods for use during dry pe
 riods. Storing water beneath the ground provides an alternative to reservo
